Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPsi]", "+"], "   ", "inward", " ", 
   "integration"}], 
  TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"355a097e-67e1-4358-8138-fd150f23d8cb"]], \
"Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.992076524827373*^9, 3.992076537639977*^9}, {
  3.9921429464072227`*^9, 3.992142949682518*^9}, {3.9925096119036407`*^9, 
  3.9925096150455637`*^9}, {3.992509676711035*^9, 3.992509676711117*^9}, {
  3.994826429187882*^9, 
  3.994826432416541*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f13c3ed8-e1a5-4349-bd70-\
380349b3f489"],

Cell["\<\
Construct the outer (+) Hertz - potential solution by imposing asymptotic \
boundary data at a large but finite radius .
The retarded Weyl scalar mode \[Psi]Ret[l, m][r] is assumed to be available \
only on a finite numerical domain, e . g . up to rDataMax .
Rather than imposing artificial zero boundary conditions at a sequence of \
increasingly large radii, 
we fit the large - r behaviour of \[Psi]Ret to a peeling expansion \
\[Psi]Ret[l, m] (r)~Sum[a_q r^(-q), q >= 5] .
Since in the outgoing - coordinate convention D = \[PartialD]_r the radial \
inversion relation is \[PartialD]_r^4\\bar\[CapitalPsi][l, m] (r) = 2 (-1)^m \
\[Psi]Ret[l, m] (r), 
the fitted \[Psi]Ret tail can be integrated analytically four times to obtain \
asymptotic values for\\bar\[CapitalPsi] and its first three r - derivatives \
at a finite matching radius rBoundary inside the numerical domain . The ODE \
is then solved inward from rBoundary down to the requested radius rEval, \
typically rmax . 
This avoids evaluating \[Psi]Ret outside its numerical domain and replaces \
the slow - converging finite - radius zero conditions with asymptotically \
consistent boundary data . 
   
   Main routines : 
   -FitPsi0RetTail[l, m, ...] Fits \[Psi]Ret[l, m] on the specified large - r \
interval to a power - law tail.
  - PsiBarTailDerivsFromFit[fit, k, r] Returns the kth r - derivative of the \
analytically integrated Hertz potential tail at radius r .
    
- PsiBarPlusSolveOne[l, m, rEval, ...] Solves \[PartialD]_r^4\\bar\
\[CapitalPsi] = 2 (-1)^m \[Psi]Ret inward from rBoundary to rEval .
- PsiBarPlusBoundaryData[l, m, rEval, ...] Returns\\bar\[CapitalPsi], \\bar\
\[CapitalPsi]', \\bar\[CapitalPsi]'', and\\bar\[CapitalPsi]''' at rEval for \
one mode . 
-PsiBarPlusBoundaryDataAll[rEval, lmax, ...] Computes the same boundary data \
for all modes 2 <= l <= lmax and - l <= m <= l . I

Important consistency checks : 
-The fitted residual \[Psi]Ret - \[Psi]RetTail should be small on the fit \
interval . 
-If \[Psi]Ret still contains an oscillatory phase at large r, first \
demodulate by the appropriate exp (\[PlusMinus]i \[Omega] r_*) factor before \
fitting the power tail .\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{27, 10}, {7, 8}},
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.992510116568512*^9, 3.992510229395028*^9}, 
   3.9945069791215343`*^9, {3.9945070101815*^9, 
   3.994507010389659*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b58745fa-279b-4591-8050-\
54b7847cd145"],

